    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\n`:che vim.ui.img` should be moved into `:che vim.health` because:\r\n- The entire module only checks a single thing (plus a static warning if tmux is detected):\r\n  <img width=\"865\" height=\"561\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/efbcb7f7-9da5-4a96-b994-dc0985505634\" />\r\n- Checking for graphics protocol support is just a check for a terminal capability, suggesting that this check belongs under the \"Terminal\" section of `vim.health`.\r\n- Warning about `tmux` belongs under the \"tmux\" section of `vim.health`.\r\n- Unlike `vim.pack`, `vim.lsp`, and `vim.treesitter`, which are all features which get their own healthchecks, `vim.ui.img` is neither a core plugin nor an api that is useful to users; it is only for plugin developers.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nMove check under `vim.health`:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"865\" height=\"561\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7e8fde4f-e869-4846-ae99-94624d5c96b7\" />\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-17T11:09:04Z",
